Hi,

The problem that caused unite() to fail was that you gave it a `list` object instead of a `methylRawList`. Using a for-loop to process the single BAM files is fine, as long as the final list will be converted into a methylRawList.

The recommended way to use multiple files with processBismarkAln would be to pass a list (!) of locations, sample.ids and a treatment vector, directly creating a methylRawList (see examples at the functions help <https://rdrr.io/bioc/methylKit/man/processBismarkAln-methods.html>).

Best,
Alex

